        <groundspeak:log id="684903976">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-08T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="553001">Bearberrys Cub</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP687 Shilo's Cap

N 50° 34.552 W 113° 51.187&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;After finding the new Calgary brass cap, I headed south to look for a few caches that while not new, were new since 2014.  Temperatures were great and the sun was shining so what better thing to do than geocache.  Quick find.  OFTH has been emailed with the information.  TFTBC&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="684684020">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-07T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="3061435">Iron Phoenix</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP687 - Shilo's Cap&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Out for yet another day of capping and caching with OBA, this time in Lethbridge!! &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_big.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; Along the way there and back. &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_wink.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; Quick find in the grass! Good thing since it's getting even cooler out after the rain has passed overhead! &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_shock.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_blackeye.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; A bit of a tight squeeze, but I think I got a pic of all the info... and the few marks on top. &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_blackeye.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; TFTCap!!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
